  "worked_solution": "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=1$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have a strict inequality, we use dashed lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/3e5663e03b92fc2be3deea9480f5314cff001cab66bfc7242837f72fbd825b69.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/a143baf42225cd4959987aa1e12abab084e4949092c7c18a1a4a2ec401cf744c.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x-1)$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(0,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(2,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(0,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(2,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)>0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041262/assets/fd46cb5d9bd91bc73bd152ca41e55ca32ba8af67870c132c906d63bb32f7c961.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
